WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.064 --> 00:00:02.054
- [Narrator] In Mexico
City, cars are everywhere.

00:00:02.054 --> 00:00:04.793
Over 3.5 million to be exact

00:00:04.793 --> 00:00:07.207
and it's not exactly
great for the environment,

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.765
but fear not, because there's a solution

00:00:09.765 --> 00:00:12.560
that can change all of that,
and that solution is a...

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.393
(record scratch)

00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:15.099
Volkswagen Beetle?

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:17.682
(joyful music)

00:00:19.123 --> 00:00:21.600
Welcome to Alto Rendimiento Automotriz.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.187
A mechanical workshop that
specializes in transforming

00:00:24.187 --> 00:00:27.400
old, gas fueled cars, into electric cars.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.177
- We started this project 10 years ago,

00:00:30.177 --> 00:00:32.694
and have converted over two dozen

00:00:32.694 --> 00:00:36.861
different (gas) vehicles
into electric ones.

00:00:38.409 --> 00:00:41.686
Our oldest converted car has been working

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:43.603
for five years nonstop.

00:00:44.923 --> 00:00:46.526
- [Narrator] Alvaro De
La Paz is the engineer

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:49.524
behind the car conversion,
and then there's Hector.

00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:52.591
- My name is Hector Ruiz, and
I'm a computer scientist.

00:00:52.591 --> 00:00:54.213
- [Narrator] Hector is
responsible for gathering

00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:56.326
the electrical parts and
making sure they work.

00:00:56.326 --> 00:00:57.159
Right?

00:00:57.159 --> 00:00:59.213
- Yeah, I do the purchasing,

00:00:59.213 --> 00:01:02.046
the extensive testing of the components.

00:01:02.046 --> 00:01:06.038
If we have to burn something, I'm the guy.

00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:09.661
In order to learn how to
do electric car conversion,

00:01:09.661 --> 00:01:11.978
you don't need any specific degree.

00:01:11.978 --> 00:01:13.482
It's something very simple.

00:01:13.482 --> 00:01:16.364
After reading a lot of books
and taking training courses,

00:01:16.364 --> 00:01:18.802
I believe anyone can do it.

00:01:18.802 --> 00:01:19.848
- [Narrator] Hector
and Alvaro learned that

00:01:19.848 --> 00:01:22.220
converting older cars
is both cost effective

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.118
and safer for the environment.

00:01:24.118 --> 00:01:27.024
- It is also far more advantageous
to convert an old car,

00:01:27.024 --> 00:01:30.305
because the older a car is,
the more fuel it uses up

00:01:30.305 --> 00:01:33.055
and the more pollution it causes.

00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:34.909
- [Narrator] By removing all the parts

00:01:34.909 --> 00:01:36.549
related to fuel combustion,

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:38.440
they can install the electrical components

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.830
to have a fully functional
electric car with zero emission.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.021
- [Alvaro] We have the
engine, which is now electric,

00:01:46.021 --> 00:01:47.790
the computer, which controls the speed,

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.124
and the battery and the battery charger.

00:01:51.124 --> 00:01:53.053
These are the main parts

00:01:53.053 --> 00:01:56.386
and they're all wired up through cables.

00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:01.712
- [Hector] This car makes me free.

00:02:01.712 --> 00:02:03.982
It's like the nirvana of the cars.

00:02:03.982 --> 00:02:06.293
You are free from gas stations;

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:09.168
you are free from the
check-up every six months.

00:02:09.168 --> 00:02:12.059
Re-usability is something
that the general public

00:02:12.059 --> 00:02:16.266
has to take into account in
order to be pollution-free.

00:02:16.266 --> 00:02:19.970
If we want to have a better
world for our children

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.269
or grandchildren, or future generations,

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:24.526
we have to be part of the solution.

00:02:24.526 --> 00:02:27.817
So, I believe the best way to
start something important

00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:32.426
for the world, at large, is
to do this kind of projects.

00:02:32.426 --> 00:02:34.759
(car honks)

